This connects directly to trustworthy AI

A trustworthy system should support calibrated trust.

There are two undesirable extremes.

Under-trust: the model is reliable, but the user doesn’t trust it.

Over-trust: the model is unreliable or uncertain, but the user trusts it anyway.

Your work is particularly relevant to over-trust.

A fluent explanation can make an answer appear more credible. If the model produces equally assertive explanations when its prediction is unstable, the explanation can increase perceived confidence without providing corresponding evidence of reliability.

So the concern isn’t merely:

“The explanation doesn’t match EBSE.”

It’s:

The explanation may cause the human’s trust to become disconnected from the model’s actual predictive reliability.

That’s much more important.

